  "notes": "Artist-producer whose signature is a massed self-harmonised vocal choir over hip-hop-derived drums. The drum claim names its lineage: \"J-Dilla-informed loose, slightly-behind programmed drums with a fat kick and a clapped or layered backbeat; percussion is stacked from many small samples rather than a single kit.\" So `snare.offGridMs` is 9 — the behind-the-beat displacement is a real number, not a feel — the humanize block is loose despite the drums being programmed, the perc lane list is five deep at a moderate density (many small samples, none loud), and the kick is fat and sparse rather than busy. The 808 is authored because the entry names it and describes an unusual relationship: \"808 sub used melodically with short glides, plus a sustained synth sub — the low end frequently moves in contrary motion to the vocal.\" That contrary motion is why `bass808` is `counter_riff` and the bassline is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.4 rather than a kick mirror: neither layer is following anything. Harmony is \"major-mode with gospel plagal cadences and added-9 voicings\" over 4-bar loops, so the IV—I family leads and `ninth` is raised. The melody and counter blocks carry the identity: \"the identity is the vocal arrangement — dozens of stacked, tuned, wide-panned self-harmony layers forming a choir that functions as the pad and the countermelody at once\", so the counter runs `sustain_pad` at the highest density ratio in this batch and the melody itself stays uncluttered, which is his stated Pixar-derived philosophy of a \"simple\" palette. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the harmonic weights and `bpm.mode` 112 (the midpoint of the stated 90—135 band) are INFERRED.",
